  "response": "# RamShield: Comprehensive Module-by-Module Remediation & Production Source Code\n\nThis document provides an in-depth audit, architectural explanation, and full production-ready code for every module in the **RamShield** high-performance DDoS mitigation and traffic intelligence engine.\n\n---\n\n## Table of Contents\n1. [Architecture Overview](#1-architecture-overview)\n2. [Module 1: `src/cache.rs` - Lock-Free Concurrent TTL Cache](#module-1-srccachers)\n3. [Module 2: `src/metrics/mod.rs` - System & Ingestion Telemetry](#module-2-srcmetricsmodrs)\n4. [Module 3: `src/storage/mod.rs` - Memory Store & Subnet Index](#module-3-srcstoragemodrs)\n5. [Module 4: `src/storage/ttl_wheel.rs` - O(1) Hierarchical Expiration Wheel](#module-4-srcstoragettl_wheelrs)\n6. [Module 5: `src/detection/mod.rs` - Ingestion Pipeline & Micro-Batching](#module-5-srcdetectionmodrs)\n7. [Module 6: `src/forecasting/mod.rs` - Holt-Winters & Shannon Entropy](#module-6-srcforecastingmodrs)\n8. [Module 7: `src/dns/forecasting/mod.rs` - DNS Attack Modeling](#module-7-srcdnsforecastingmodrs)\n9. [Module 8: `src/alerting/mod.rs` - Enterprise Auditing & Alerts](#module-8-srcalertingmodrs)\n10. [Module 9: `src/dashboard/mod.rs` - Real-Time Management REST API](#module-9-srcdashboardmodrs)\n11. [Module 10: `src/engine/mod.rs` - Core Coordinator & Pipeline Bootstrapper](#module-10-srcenginemodrs)\n12. [Module 11: `src/ipc/server.rs` - High-Throughput Framed IPC Engine](#module-11-srcipcserverrs)\n13. [Module 12: `src/cli.rs` - Type-Safe Administrative CLI](#module-12-srcclirs)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n```\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                Edge / IPC Clients                                 |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n                                          |\n                                          v  [TCP / Framed JSON Stream]\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                 IpcServer                                         |\n|   - Semaphore-governed concurrency                                               |\n|   - Bounded channel event ingestion                                              |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n                                          |\n                                          v  [Crossbeam Channel]\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                             DetectionEngine                                       |\n|   - Micro-batch pre-aggregation (IpAgg)                                           |\n|   - Subnet window accounting (/24 prefix table)                                   |\n|   - Dual-hash Bloom Filter fast path                                              |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n                                          |\n                                          v  [tokio::broadcast block_tx]\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                             Block Consumer Worker                                 |\n|   - Writes BlockState::Blocked to Store                                           |\n|   - Updates Subnet Reverse Index (DashSet)                                        |\n|   - Registers key in TtlWheel for proactive expiration                            |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n           |                                                     |\n           v                                                     v\n+------------------------------------+         +------------------------------------+\n|              Store                 |         |             TtlWheel               |\n|   - Sharded DashMap Storage        |         |   - Constant-time tick buckets     |\n|   - RAM Budget Enforcement         |         |   - Batched proactive eviction     |\n+------------------------------------+         +------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n## Module 1: `src/cache.rs`\n\n### Audit & Fixes\n1. **Atomic Counter Race in `get`**: Removed unconditional `fetch_sub` when an expired key is dropped. The decrement is now guarded by `if self.inner.remove(key).is_some()`, preventing underflow from concurrent readers.\n2. **Doc Comment Duplication**: Cleaned up duplicated doc comment blocks on `Cache::get`.\n3. **Background Evictor Resiliency**: Improved evictor loop termination and safe shard traversal.\n\n### Source Code\n```rust\n//! Thread-safe, TTL-backed concurrent cache.\n//!\n//! Backed by [`DashMap`] with a dedicated OS evictor thread for proactive pruning.\n//! Operates fully lock-free across DashMap shards.\n\nuse dashmap::DashMap;\nuse std::hash::Hash;\nuse std::sync::atomic::{AtomicBool, AtomicU64, Ordering};\nuse std::sync::Arc;\nuse std::time::{Duration, SystemTime, UNIX_EPOCH};\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\npub struct Entry<V> {\n    pub value: V,\n    pub expire: Option<u64>,\n    pub created: u64,\n}\n\nfn now_ns() -> u64 {\n    SystemTime::now()\n        .duration_since(UNIX_EPOCH)\n        .map(|d| d.as_nanos() as u64)\n        .unwrap_or(0)\n}\n\npub struct Cache<K, V> {\n    inner: Arc<DashMap<K, Entry<V>>>,\n    capacity: usize,\n    default_ttl: Duration,\n    count: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    shutdown: Arc<AtomicBool>,\n}\n\nimpl<K, V> Cache<K, V>\nwhere\n    K: Hash + Eq + Clone + Send + Sync + 'static,\n    V: Clone + Send + Sync + 'static,\n{\n    pub fn new(entry_cap: usize, default_ttl: Duration) -> Self {\n        let inner = Arc::new(DashMap::new());\n        let count = Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0));\n        let shutdown = Arc::new(AtomicBool::new(false));\n\n        Self::spawn_evictor(inner.clone(), count.clone(), shutdown.clone());\n\n        Self {\n            inner,\n            capacity: entry_cap,\n            default_ttl,\n            count,\n            shutdown,\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn spawn_evictor(\n        inner: Arc<DashMap<K, Entry<V>>>,\n        count: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n        shutdown: Arc<AtomicBool>,\n    ) {\n        let _ = std::thread::Builder::new()\n            .name(\"cache-evictor\".into())\n            .spawn(move || {\n                while !shutdown.load(Ordering::Acquire) {\n                    std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_secs(5));\n                    let now = now_ns();\n                    let mut removed = 0u64;\n                    inner.retain(|_, entry| match entry.expire {\n                        Some(exp) if now >= exp => {\n                            removed += 1;\n                            false\n                        }\n                        _ => true,\n                    });\n                    if removed > 0 {\n                        count.fetch_sub(removed, Ordering::Relaxed);\n                    }\n                }\n            });\n    }\n\n    pub fn shutdown(&self) {\n        self.shutdown.store(true, Ordering::Release);\n    }\n\n    pub fn get<'a>(&'a self, key: &'a K) -> Option<dashmap::mapref::one::Ref<'a, K, Entry<V>>> {\n        let now = now_ns();\n        let entry = self.inner.get(key)?;\n\n        if let Some(exp) = entry.expire {\n            if now >= exp {\n                drop(entry);\n                if self.inner.remove(key).is_some() {\n                    self.count.fetch_sub(1, Ordering::Relaxed);\n                }\n                return None;\n            }\n        }\n        Some(entry)\n    }\n\n    pub fn insert(&self, key: K, value: V, ttl: Option<Duration>) {\n        let ttl = ttl.unwrap_or(self.default_ttl);\n        let expire = if ttl.is_zero() {\n            None\n        } else {\n            Some(now_ns().saturating_add(ttl.as_nanos() as u64))\n        };\n\n        let entry = Entry {\n            value,\n            expire,\n            created: now_ns(),\n        };\n\n        if self.capacity > 0\n            && !self.inner.contains_key(&key)\n            && self.count.load(Ordering::Relaxed) as usize >= self.capacity\n        {\n            if let Some(victim) = self.inner.iter().next().map(|e| e.key().clone()) {\n                if self.inner.remove(&victim).is_some() {\n                    self.count.fetch_sub(1, Ordering::Relaxed);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        let old = self.inner.insert(key, entry);\n        if old.is_none() {\n            self.count.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub fn remove(&self, key: &K) -> Option<Entry<V>> {\n        let removed = self.inner.remove(key).map(|(_k, entry)| entry);\n        if removed.is_some() {\n            self.count.fetch_sub(1, Ordering::Relaxed);\n        }\n        removed\n    }\n\n    pub fn clear(&self) {\n        self.inner.clear();\n        self.count.store(0, Ordering::Relaxed);\n    }\n\n    pub fn len(&self) -> usize {\n        self.count.load(Ordering::Relaxed) as usize\n    }\n\n    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool {\n        self.len() == 0\n    }\n\n    pub fn capacity(&self) -> usize {\n        self.capacity\n    }\n}\n\nimpl<K, V> Drop for Cache<K, V> {\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\n        self.shutdown.store(true, Ordering::Release);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Module 2: `src/metrics/mod.rs`\n\n### Audit & Fixes\n1. **I/O Bottleneck**: Replaced `sys.refresh_all()` with lightweight `sys.refresh_cpu()` and `sys.refresh_memory()` calls.\n2. **Prometheus Exposition**: Ensured all metrics, gauges, and rates align with Prometheus standard types.\n3. **Safe History Deques**: Bounded `batch_history` and `block_log` rings to prevent memory bloat.\n\n### Source Code\n```rust\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\nuse std::collections::VecDeque;\nuse std::sync::atomic::{AtomicU64, Ordering};\nuse std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};\nuse std::time::{SystemTime, UNIX_EPOCH};\nuse sysinfo::{CpuExt, System, SystemExt};\n\nconst HISTORY: usize = 80;\nconst BLOCK_LOG: usize = 40;\n\npub fn now_ms() -> u64 {\n    SystemTime::now()\n        .duration_since(UNIX_EPOCH)\n        .unwrap_or_default()\n        .as_millis() as u64\n}\n\nfn with_system<F, R>(f: F) -> R\nwhere\n    F: FnOnce(&mut System) -> R,\n{\n    static SYS: Mutex<Option<System>> = Mutex::new(None);\n    let mut guard = SYS.lock().unwrap();\n    if guard.is_none() {\n        let mut sys = System::new();\n        sys.refresh_cpu();\n        sys.refresh_memory();\n        *guard = Some(sys);\n    }\n    f(guard.as_mut().unwrap())\n}\n\npub fn get_system_usage() -> (f32, usize) {\n    with_system(|sys| {\n        sys.refresh_cpu();\n        sys.refresh_memory();\n        let cpu_usage = sys.global_cpu_info().cpu_usage();\n        let total_memory_mb = (sys.used_memory() as f64 / 1024.0 / 1024.0) as usize;\n        (cpu_usage, total_memory_mb)\n    })\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct BatchRecord {\n    pub ts_ms: u64,\n    pub events: u32,\n    pub unique_ips: u32,\n    pub promoted: u32,\n    pub cold_skipped: u32,\n    pub promoted_events: u32,\n    pub cold_skipped_events: u32,\n    pub blocks: u32,\n    pub hot_subnets: u32,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct BlockRecord {\n    pub ts_ms: u64,\n    pub ip: String,\n    pub reason: String,\n    pub module: String,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct ModuleStats {\n    pub label: String,\n    pub events: u64,\n    pub errors: u64,\n    pub rate_per_sec: f64,\n    pub detail: serde_json::Value,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct DashboardSnapshot {\n    pub ts_ms: u64,\n    pub uptime_secs: u64,\n    pub ips_tracked: usize,\n    pub blocked_total: u64,\n    pub ram_bytes: usize,\n    pub ram_limit_mb: usize,\n    pub ram_pct: f64,\n    pub cpu_usage: f32,\n    pub memory_usage_mb: usize,\n    pub ipc_requests: u64,\n    pub events_ingested: u64,\n    pub events_rejected: u64,\n    pub channel_depth: usize,\n    pub batches_total: u64,\n    pub promotions: u64,\n    pub cold_skipped: u64,\n    pub blocks_applied: u64,\n    pub pipeline: PipelineFlow,\n    pub is_healthy: bool,\n    pub health_reason: String,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct SubnetRow {\n    pub prefix: String,\n    pub events: u64,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\npub struct PipelineFlow {\n    pub ingest: u64,\n    pub queued: u64,\n    pub batched: u64,\n    pub promoted: u64,\n    pub merged: u64,\n    pub blocked: u64,\n}\n\npub struct Metrics {\n    pub requests_total: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub blocks_total: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub events_ingested: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub events_rejected: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub batches_total: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub promotions_total: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub cold_skipped_total: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub blocks_detection: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub blocks_subnet: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub blocks_forecast: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub forecast_ticks: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub entropy_ticks: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub hw_rps_bits: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub hw_z_bits: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub hw_forecast_bits: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub entropy_bits: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub last_batch_events: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub last_batch_promoted: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub last_batch_blocks: Arc<AtomicU64>,\n    pub last_batch: Arc<Mutex<Option<BatchRecord>>>,\n    pub batch_history: Arc<Mutex<VecDeque<BatchRecord>>>,\n    pub block_log: Arc<Mutex<VecDeque<BlockRecord>>>,\n    started_ms: u64,\n}\n\nimpl Metrics {\n    pub fn new() -> Self {\n        Self {\n            requests_total: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            blocks_total: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            events_ingested: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            events_rejected: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            batches_total: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            promotions_total: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            cold_skipped_total: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            blocks_detection: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            blocks_subnet: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            blocks_forecast: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            forecast_ticks: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            entropy_ticks: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            hw_rps_bits: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            hw_z_bits: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            hw_forecast_bits: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            entropy_bits: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            last_batch_events: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            last_batch_promoted: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            last_batch_blocks: Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0)),\n            last_batch: Arc::new(Mutex::new(None)),\n            batch_history: Arc::new(Mutex::new(VecDeque::with_capacity(HISTORY))),\n            block_log: Arc::new(Mutex::new(VecDeque::with_capacity(BLOCK_LOG))),\n            started_ms: now_ms(),\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub fn inc_requests(&self) {\n        self.requests_total.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);\n    }\n    pub fn inc_blocks(&self) {\n        self.blocks_total.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);\n    }\n    pub fn inc_ingested(&self, n: u64) {\n        self.events_ingested.fetch_add(n, Ordering::Relaxed);\n    }\n    pub fn inc_rejected(&self, n: u64) {\n        self.events_rejected.fetch_add(n, Ordering::Relaxed);\n    }\n\n    pub fn record_batch(&self, rec: BatchRecord) {\n        self.batches_total.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);\n        self.last_batch_events.store(rec.events as u64, Ordering::Relaxed);\n        self.last_batch_promoted.store(rec.promoted as u64, Ordering::Relaxed);\n        self.last_batch_blocks.store(rec.blocks as u64, Ordering::Relaxed);\n        self.promotions_total.fetch_add(rec.promoted as u64, Ordering::Relaxed);\n        self.cold_skipped_total.fetch_add(rec.cold_skipped as u64, Ordering::Relaxed);\n        if let Ok(mut h) = self.batch_history.lock() {\n            if h.len() >= HISTORY {\n                h.pop_front();\n            }\n            h.push_back(rec.clone());\n        }\n        if let Ok(mut lb) = self.last_batch.lock() {\n            *lb = Some(rec);\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub fn record_block(&self, ip: &str, reason: &str, module: &str) {\n        self.blocks_total.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);\n        match module {\n            \"detection\" => { self.blocks_detection.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed); }\n            \"subnet\" => { self.blocks_subnet.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed); }\n            \"forecast\" | \"forecasting\" => { self.blocks_forecast.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed); }\n            _ => {}\n        }\n        if let Ok(mut log) = self.block_log.lock() {\n            if log.len() >= BLOCK_LOG {\n                log.pop_front();\n            }\n            log.push_back(BlockRecord {\n                ts_ms: now_ms(),\n                ip: ip.to_string(),\n                reason: reason.to_string(),\n                module: module.to_string(),\n            });\n        }\n    }\n\n    pub fn set_forecast_hw(&self, rps: f64, z: f64, forecast: f64) {\n        self.hw_rps_bits.store(rps.to_bits(), Ordering::Relaxed);\n        self.hw_z_bits.store(z.to_bits(), Ordering::Relaxed);\n        self.hw_forecast_bits.store(forecast.to_bits(), Ordering::Relaxed);\n        self.forecast_ticks.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);\n    }\n\n    pub fn set_entropy(&self, h: f64) {\n        self.entropy_bits.store(h.to_bits(), Ordering::Relaxed);\n        self.entropy_ticks.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);\n    }\n\n    fn f64(bits: &AtomicU64) -> f64 {\n        f64::from_bits(bits.load(Ordering::Relaxed))\n    }\n\n    pub fn get_batch_history(&self) -> Vec<BatchRecord> {\n        self.batch_history\n            .lock()\n            .map(|h| h.iter().cloned().collect())\n            .unwrap_or_default()\n    }\n\n    pub fn get_block_log(&self) -> Vec<BlockRecord> {\n        self.block_log\n            .lock()\n            .map(|h| h.iter().cloned().collect())\n            .unwrap_or_default()\n    }\n\n    pub fn get_module_stats_data(\n        &self,\n        _uptime_secs: u64,\n        ingested: u64,\n        _channel_depth: usize,\n        ips_tracked: usize,\n        ram_bytes: usize,\n        ram_limit_mb: usize,\n    ) -> Vec<ModuleStats> {\n        let elapsed = ((now_ms().saturating_sub(self.started_ms)) as f64 / 1000.0).max(0.001);\n        let batches = self.batches_total.load(Ordering::Relaxed);\n\n        let hw_rps = Metrics::f64(&self.hw_rps_bits);\n        let hw_z = Metrics::f64(&self.hw_z_bits);\n        let hw_f = Metrics::f64(&self.hw_forecast_bits);\n        let entropy = Metrics::f64(&self.entropy_bits);\n        let last_ev = self.last_batch_events.load(Ordering::Relaxed);\n        let (_cpu_usage, total_system_memory_mb) = get_system_usage();\n\n        vec![\n            ModuleStats {\n                label: \"IPC\".into(),\n                events: self.requests_total.load(Ordering::Relaxed),\n                errors: self.events_rejected.load(Ordering::Relaxed),\n                rate_per_sec: self.requests_total.load(Ordering::Relaxed) as f64 / elapsed,\n                detail: serde_json::json!({\n                    \"ingested\": ingested,\n                    \"rejected\": self.events_rejected.load(Ordering::Relaxed),\n                }),\n            },\n            ModuleStats {\n                label: \"Detection\".into(),\n                events: ingested,\n                errors: 0,\n                rate_per_sec: ingested as f64 / elapsed,\n                detail: serde_json::json!({\n                    \"batches\": batches,\n                    \"promotions\": self.promotions_total.load(Ordering::Relaxed),\n                    \"cold_skipped\": self.cold_skipped_total.